# Counts rather than the set itself: answering with the set would mean
# loading a page of it — a progress block and an accession summary per row
# — for a body the client re-reads anyway.
#
# Both numbers, because "8 added" alone leaves somebody who checked ten
# wondering what happened to the other two.
{
  added:          @added,
  already_in_set: @already_in_set
}
